# The build context is the repo root, and the repo root contains 691 MB of live runtime
# state. Without this file every `docker build` uploads the catalogue, the 255 MB spend
# ledger and every dossier to the daemon before the first instruction runs — and worse,
# `COPY . /app` would bake a point-in-time copy of the store INTO the image, where it
# would shadow the volume mount for anything that resolved a path before the mount.
#
# The store is state. It arrives on the volume, never in the image.
store/
storage/
signals/pending/
graphify-out/

# Build outputs and dependency trees. The image installs its own.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/bin/
**/obj/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local-only. `.env` in particular must never be baked in: secrets reach the container
# through `fly secrets` or compose's env_file, both of which keep them out of the image
# layers and out of anything that can be pulled.
.env
.env.*
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.lux/keys/
*.log

# Documentation and tests are not needed at runtime and are the bulk of the remaining
# context. The tests still run in CI against the repo, not against the image.
docs/
specs/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
